    {
        "id": "comment_1",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "multi_adc_example",
        "name": "Multi-ADC Comparison Node Demo",
        "info": "This flow demonstrates the multi-ADC comparison node:\n\n1. **Configure Multiple Sensors:** The node is set up to monitor 4 different sensors:\n   - Temperature sensor on AIN0 (single-ended, gain=1)\n   - Pressure sensor on AIN1 (single-ended, gain=2) \n   - Voltage differential between AIN2 and AIN3 (differential, gain=4)\n   - Current sensor on AIN4 (single-ended, gain=8)\n\n2. **Round-Robin Processing:** The node processes each comparison in sequence\n\n3. **Aggregated Output:** Results from all comparisons are delivered together at 2Hz\n\n4. **Individual Settings:** Each comparison has its own gain, buffer, and sample rate settings\n\n**Controls:**\n- Start Monitoring: Begin continuous measurement\n- Stop Monitoring: Stop all measurements\n- Get Status: Check current node status\n\n**Output Format:**\n```json\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2025-09-12T14:30:00.000Z\",\n  \"measurements\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Temperature Sensor\",\n      \"channel\": 0,\n      \"raw\": 2097152,\n      \"mV\": 625.0,\n      \"config\": { ... }\n    },\n    // ... more measurements\n  ],\n  \"cycleStats\": {\n    \"totalCycleTime\": 45.2,\n    \"samplesPerComparison\": 1,\n    \"emissionFrequency\": 2.0\n  }\n}\n```",
        "x": 610,
        "y": 120,
        "wires": []
    }
]
